Review these previously model-flagged conflict pairs against the supplied quotations and scope/date fields. Do not assume every pair is a conflict. Different products, origins, tariff programs, or dated stages are not automatically contradictory. Only use apparent_same_scope_conflict when the supplied claims appear incompatible on the same scope/date; otherwise distinguish dated progression, differing scope, complementary claims, and missing scope. Do not verify current law from memory. Explain the reason briefly for every pair.
UNTRUSTED_EVIDENCE_JSON:
{"research_date": "2026-09-10", "pairs": [{"pair_id": "conflict_fb1bb3b7bdc1703021a58391", "claim_ids": ["claim_0fef2f438ea732466143ab88", "claim_5ac65fe04bd8630f9f391091"], "query_ids": ["q_466"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_0fef2f438ea732466143ab88", "quote": "No drawback shall be available with respect to the duties imposed pursuant to this proclamation.", "url": "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/adjusting-imports-of-automobiles-and-autombile-parts-into-the-united-states", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_5ac65fe04bd8630f9f391091", "quote": "No drawback is available with respect to the additional duties imposed pursuant to the Presidential Proclamation 10908, as implemented in the FRN 90 FR 14705.", "url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHSCBP/bulletins/3de7ef9", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_c3ab7dffa18f3f056754f3d7", "claim_ids": ["claim_e7afc8d9427a96e6ab8a4d87", "claim_f2c978a5819dd2c90435cb62"], "query_ids": ["q_466"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_e7afc8d9427a96e6ab8a4d87", "quote": "Any automobile or automobile part, except those eligible for admission under “domestic status” as defined in 19 CFR 146.43, that is subject to the duty imposed by this proclamation and that is admitted into a United States foreign trade zone on or after the effective date of this proclamation, in accordance with clause (1) of this proclamation, must be admitted as “privileged foreign status” as defined in 19 CFR 146.41, and will be subject upon entry for consumption to any ad valorem rates of duty related to the classification under the applicable HTSUS subheading.", "url": "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/adjusting-imports-of-automobiles-and-autombile-parts-into-the-united-states", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "duty imposed by this proclamation", "affected_product": "automobile or automobile part"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_f2c978a5819dd2c90435cb62", "quote": "Any automobile parts, except those that are eligible for admission to a foreign trade zone under “domestic status” as defined in 19 CFR 146.43 and are admitted into a United States foreign trade zone on or after 12:01 a.m. ET on May 3, 2025, must be admitted as “privileged foreign status” as defined in 19 CFR 146.41.", "url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHSCBP/bulletins/3de7ef9", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "foreign trade zone"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_3d7a7766a74b50fa664f7777", "claim_ids": ["claim_03f619fb07cd24e7aa51f9ad", "claim_dc422b1532b11556e4e4f9c6"], "query_ids": ["q_467"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_03f619fb07cd24e7aa51f9ad", "quote": "Moreover, if goods are exported from an FTZ, no duties are paid at all, providing a clear financial incentive for companies engaged in international trade.", "url": "https://rklogisticsgroup.com/ftz-tariff-mitigation-battery-energy-storage", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "FTZ"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_dc422b1532b11556e4e4f9c6", "quote": "Duty Elimination: No customs duties are due on merchandise exported directly from the FTZ. Duty can also be eliminated on goods destroyed in an FTZ, waste or scrap.", "url": "https://www.wtcsavannah.org/foreign-trade-zone-benefits-for-business", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_28ec8b52ecd4623d4d6f08da", "claim_ids": ["claim_003581fe3505122551f29ace", "claim_b6a6065337c35f9db1f22fb6"], "query_ids": ["q_467"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_003581fe3505122551f29ace", "quote": "These designated areas within the United States allow for the deferral, reduction, or elimination of customs duties on imported goods, which can significantly impact the bottom line for companies dealing with high-value components such as lithium-ion batteries and advanced energy storage systems.", "url": "https://rklogisticsgroup.com/ftz-tariff-mitigation-battery-energy-storage", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Foreign-Trade Zones (FTZs)", "affected_product": "lithium-ion batteries and advanced energy storage systems", "duty_rate": "deferral, reduction, or elimination of customs duties"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_b6a6065337c35f9db1f22fb6", "quote": "FTZs offer a unique advantage by allowing goods to be admitted duty-free until they leave the zone for domestic consumption.", "url": "https://rklogisticsgroup.com/ftz-tariff-mitigation-battery-energy-storage", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Foreign-Trade Zones (FTZs)"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_44b584169b7789b4cbece9de", "claim_ids": ["claim_3e38667896c591526b07a1d1", "claim_46e529414dbc94e22ecba67f"], "query_ids": ["q_468"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_3e38667896c591526b07a1d1", "quote": "The tariff rate for non-lithium-ion battery parts will increase from 7.5% to 25% in 2024.", "url": "https://www.wiley.law/alert-Biden-Administration-Seeks-to-Increase-Section-301-Duties-on-Imports-from-China", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"affected_product": "non-lithium-ion battery parts", "duty_rate": "7.5% to 25%", "effective_date": "in 2024"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_46e529414dbc94e22ecba67f", "quote": "These tariff increases will take effect on January 1, 2025. See FRN 89 FR 101682.", "url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHSCBP/bulletins/3ca1cf1", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"effective_date": "January 1, 2025"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_459e9719f365183aca482a5a", "claim_ids": ["claim_46e529414dbc94e22ecba67f", "claim_7c3ed294da9e8e1338f9cd93"], "query_ids": ["q_468"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_46e529414dbc94e22ecba67f", "quote": "These tariff increases will take effect on January 1, 2025. See FRN 89 FR 101682.", "url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHSCBP/bulletins/3ca1cf1", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"effective_date": "January 1, 2025"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_7c3ed294da9e8e1338f9cd93", "quote": "Batteries and Battery Components and Parts: The tariff rate for lithium-ion EV batteries will increase from 7.5% to 25% in 2024.", "url": "https://www.wiley.law/alert-Biden-Administration-Seeks-to-Increase-Section-301-Duties-on-Imports-from-China", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"affected_product": "lithium-ion EV batteries", "duty_rate": "7.5% to 25%", "effective_date": "in 2024"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_fdfd98b5dd3104e9916231cc", "claim_ids": ["claim_13ee4278b98b7da760a23de7", "claim_5641f7967979db2ed56cc191"], "query_ids": ["q_469"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_13ee4278b98b7da760a23de7", "quote": "electric vehicles to 100 percent, semiconductors to 50 percent from January 1, 2025, and EV lithium-ion batteries to 25 percent (USTR, 2024).", "url": "https://www.platton.ai/insights/warehouse-and-fulfilment/mitigating-tariff-impacts-bonded-warehouses-ftz", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301 action on Chinese imports", "affected_product": "electric vehicles", "duty_rate": "100 percent", "effective_date": "January 1, 2025"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_5641f7967979db2ed56cc191", "quote": "The Section 301 action on Chinese imports, finalized in the US Trade Representative's September 2024 four-year review, kept Lists 1 through 4A at 7.5 to 25 percent", "url": "https://www.platton.ai/insights/warehouse-and-fulfilment/mitigating-tariff-impacts-bonded-warehouses-ftz", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301 action on Chinese imports", "duty_rate": "7.5 to 25 percent", "announcement_date": "September 2024"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_6b34580cad6c6d6dae7f0a1e", "claim_ids": ["claim_3bbbf600bcb6e13d3d5bde25", "claim_e96052c1a30f027ed5f57c94"], "query_ids": ["q_470"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_3bbbf600bcb6e13d3d5bde25", "quote": "CBP's published position: Section 301 duties are recoverable through drawback, up to 99 percent. No proclamation bars it.", "url": "https://gingercontrol.com/resources/duty-drawback", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301 (China lists)", "legal_authority": "CSMS #18-000419; 19 U.S.C. 1313", "duty_rate": "up to 99 percent"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_e96052c1a30f027ed5f57c94", "quote": "Section 301 duties are recoverable through drawback, up to 99 percent. No proclamation bars it.", "url": "https://gingercontrol.com/resources/duty-drawback", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301 (China lists)", "duty_rate": "up to 99 percent", "reported_policy_status": "Yes"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_9bf985b7889db1093e9a97f3", "claim_ids": ["claim_d614cb9f85293c735bb7590a", "claim_fb861afa60932db092282016"], "query_ids": ["q_471"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_d614cb9f85293c735bb7590a", "quote": "Failure to export or destroy the articles in accordance with the regulations within the appropriate period of time will result in liquidated damages.", "url": "https://www.cbp.gov/trade/programs-administration/entry-summary-and-post-release-processes/temporary-importation-under-bond", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_fb861afa60932db092282016", "quote": "Failing to export or destroy the goods on time? That triggers liquidated damages, typically equal to twice the estimated duties.", "url": "https://www.customsmanager.info/post/us-tib-temporary-imports-under-bond", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "twice the estimated duties"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_ae16fcf4c1401d7f53af5de1", "claim_ids": ["claim_12a44833e9bcd8e52e93bde4", "claim_3cfb44f0b2ca5518534bcf24"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_12a44833e9bcd8e52e93bde4", "quote": "Carrington Co. v. United States, the Court of Customs and Patent Appeals (“CCPA”) said “it is a well-established principle that classification of an imported article must rest upon its condition as imported.”", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "Carrington Co. v. United States"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_3cfb44f0b2ca5518534bcf24", "quote": "Simod America Corp. v. United States, noting that “imported merchandise is dutiable in its condition as imported, except in the instance … of deception, disguise, or artifice resorted to for the purpose of perpetrating a fraud of the revenue", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "Simod America Corp. v. United States"}}]}]}

